::MCQ::
Which function converts a JSON string to a Python dictionary?
{
~ json.convert()
= json.loads()
~ json.decode()
~ json.parse()
}

::MCQ::
What types of data can json.loads() directly convert?
{
~ Only strings
~ Dictionaries
= str, bytes, bytearray
~ Lists and tuples
}

::MCQ::
How do you create a custom JSON encoder in Python?
{
~ By creating a function
~ By using a lambda function
~ By modifying the json module
= By subclassing json.JSONEncoder
}

::MCQ::
Which JSON data types are supported?
{
= string, number, boolean, nested json, arrays, null
~ integers, floats, tuples, sets
~ classes, functions, modules
~ datetime objects, complex numbers
}

::MCQ::
json.dumps() converts a Python dictionary to a JSON string.
{
= True
~ False
}
